{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem","title":"thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.md","line":741,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.tex#thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-submanifold-connectivity]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-diameter]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#def:pet-ch6-l-connected]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.tex","label":"thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem","line":1614,"source":"\\begin{theorem}[Berger's sphere theorem]\n  \\label{thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem}\n\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0279}\n  \\uses{thm:pet-ch6-submanifold-connectivity, lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-diameter, def:pet-ch6-l-connected}\n  \\dcref{ch6:6.5.4}\n  Let $M$ be a closed $n$-manifold with $\\sec\\ge1$. If $\\operatorname{inj}_p>\\pi/2$ for\n  some $p\\in M$, then $M$ is $(n-1)$-connected, hence a homotopy sphere.\n\\end{theorem}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{thm:pet-ch6-submanifold-connectivity, lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-diameter}\n  \\sketch\n  At a point \\(p\\), loops have length \\(>\\pi\\) and the Bonnet--Synge variation gives \\(n-1\\) negative directions. By \\cref{thm:pet-ch6-submanifold-connectivity}, \\(\\{p\\}\\subset M\\) is \\((n-1)\\)-connected; a degree-one map to \\(S^n\\), Hurewicz, and Whitehead give a homotopy sphere.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Theorem</div></section>[Berger&#x27;s sphere theorem] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-74686d3a7065742d6368362d6265726765722d7370686572652d7468656f72656d\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0279</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23thm%3Apet-ch6-submanifold-connectivity\">↗ thm:pet-ch6-submanifold-connectivity</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23lem%3Apet-ch6-bonnet-synge-diameter\">↗ lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-diameter</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23def%3Apet-ch6-l-connected\">↗ def:pet-ch6-l-connected</a> <span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch6:6.5.4</span></span>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> be a closed <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n$\">$n$</span>-manifold with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\sec \\ge 1$\">$\\sec \\ge 1$</span>. If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {inj}_p&gt;\\pi /2$\">$\\operatorname {inj}_p&gt;\\pi /2$</span> for some <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(n-1)$\">$(n-1)$</span>-connected, hence a homotopy sphere.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23thm%3Apet-ch6-submanifold-connectivity\">↗ thm:pet-ch6-submanifold-connectivity</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23lem%3Apet-ch6-bonnet-synge-diameter\">↗ lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-diameter</a> \\sketch At a point <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span>, loops have length <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$&gt;\\pi $\">$&gt;\\pi $</span> and the Bonnet–Synge variation gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n-1$\">$n-1$</span> negative directions. By <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23thm%3Apet-ch6-submanifold-connectivity\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-submanifold-connectivity\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-74686d3a7065742d6368362d7375626d616e69666f6c642d636f6e6e6563746976697479\">section 5</a>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\{ p\\} \\subset M$\">$\\{ p\\} \\subset M$</span> is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(n-1)$\">$(n-1)$</span>-connected; a degree-one map to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$S^n$\">$S^n$</span>, Hurewicz, and Whitehead give a homotopy sphere. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-submanifold-connectivity","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-klingenberg-pinching-injectivity","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-submanifold-connectivity","title":"thm:pet-ch6-submanifold-connectivity","label":"thm:p